## Summary
Lee Jun-seok has resigned as the leader of the Reform Party, citing a lack of response to his party reform initiatives. This resignation underscores internal challenges within the party in achieving consensus on reforms.

## Key Points
- Lee Jun-seok stepped down from his position as leader of the Reform Party.
- The resignation was attributed to the failure to garner sufficient support for party reforms.
- This event may signal broader internal divisions or resistance to change within the party.


